    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (2/2 tests pass, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `membershipTier` field is exposed on `GET /api/owners/{id}` (which flows through `RespondWithOwner` \u2192 `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`). Two edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct mapping expression:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"membershipTier\",\n       expression = \"java(owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0 \"\n               + \"&& owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank() ? \\\"SILVER\\\" : \\\"BRONZE\\\")\")\n   ```\n\nThis returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` and an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE` \u2014 matching both new acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`). The null guards keep it safe for owners where those fields aren't populated. No `@RestController` was introduced; the endpoint remains the existing OfficeFloor pipeline.",
