    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe new `membershipTier` mapping sits directly beside the existing expression-based `membershipNumber` mapping in the same `OwnerMapper` interface. It follows the file's established convention exactly: a derived DTO field expressed as an inline `@Mapping(expression = ...)` computed from `Owner` fields. That is precisely what a MapStruct mapper is for \u2014 deriving DTO fields from the entity \u2014 so the logic is in the right unit, and a maintainer of this file would find the placement and style natural rather than surprising.\n\n- No duplication: the rule appears once, in the mapper, and once as documentation in the OpenAPI schema (the appropriate place for the contract).\n- The mapper interface isn't becoming a catch-all \u2014 mapping owner\u2192DTO fields is its single responsibility, and this is one more such field.\n- The OpenAPI addition is additive and consistent with the neighboring `membershipNumber`/count properties (title/description/type/example/readOnly), matching the schema's existing shape.\n\nThe inline ternary is on the denser side, but it mirrors the equally-complex `membershipNumber` expression right above it, so it's consistent with the surrounding code rather than an outlier. Structure is clean and additive.",
